      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can Cloudflare managed robots.txt contradict my own robots.txt?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, while the Instruct AI bot traffic with robots.txt toggle is enabled, Cloudflare prepends a managed block above your authored file, and that block can allow or disallow bots differently from your own rules until you disable the injection.</p></details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is the managed robots.txt served identically to every client?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No, we observed conditional serving on our own zone: a crawler user agent received the managed block while a desktop browser user agent saw only our authored file, which is why verification must always use a crawler user agent.</p></details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I block AI crawlers on the Cloudflare free plan?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, the managed robots.txt feature and basic custom WAF rules are available on free plans; Super Bot Fight Mode requires a paid plan, and advanced rate limiting depends on your tier.</p></details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Will WAF rules that block AI bots affect Googlebot?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No, not when scoped correctly: match AI crawler tokens such as GPTBot and ClaudeBot or their ASNs, never all bot traffic, and Googlebot continues to crawl normally.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
